WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
SPEAKER: One of the
essentials of citizenship

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:05.640
is a presence or the
creation and the preservation

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.885
of a large middle class.

00:00:06.885 --> 00:00:09.870
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.960
This idea goes all the way back
to Greece where citizenship

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.180
first developed, and they
had a word for it, the mesoi,

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.090
M-E-S-O-I. In their
way of thinking,

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:26.280
you had to have the majority
of citizens self-employed,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.170
independent, outspoken,
and neither rich nor poor.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.490
The middle class alone were
neither dependent on the state

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:40.260
nor did they emulate or
do they envy the rich.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.280
And so these mesoi and the
idealized Greek city-state

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.220
were the citizens that showed
up in the assembly hall,

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:53.520
they were outside, and they had
an equal seat on stone benches.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.240
That equality was reflected
in the military sense

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.950
by slots and the phalanx.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.890
That is the armed
squares of Spearman

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.340
that fought the battles
of the city-state.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.670
And finally, there was a third
dimension of the middle class

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.120
and that was the agrarian
grid outside the city-state.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.000
Most land was parceled as
it was during the Homestead

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.020
Act in the United States
into 10 acre parcels.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.640
The citizen also had
to be independent.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.090
They were in control of the
laws, they made the laws,

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.300
and they were not
subject to coercion

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.280
from the poor or the rich.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.920
There's another idea that comes
from the ancient world that's

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.990
important to remember that
something about being in charge

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:42.060
of your own destiny combines
the mental with the physical.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.760
And by that, I mean in
the pre-industrial world

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.830
most people were farmers.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.840
So they would get
up in the morning

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.720
and they would
prune vines or they

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.290
would have to plant olive
trees or in the spring,

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:57.030
they would cut
grain or thresh it,

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.970
but it was a
constant physical job

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.980
but yet they were
making decisions.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.570
It was a mental task.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:06.120
And to the Greeks,
this combination

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.030
of mental acuity and
physical strength

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.710
made the perfect balance.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.860
Now, we all can't
be farmers today.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.530
Only 1% of the
nation farms, but we

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.480
have all of these tasks today.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.860
The independent
trucker, think about it.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.890
He has to have endurance to
get on that highway for 16,

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:28.290
17 hours, but yet, he has to
make the decisions, which job

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.140
shall I take, how much
does diesel fuel cost,

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.260
and the same thing holds
true of the business person.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.180
If you work for
a corporation you

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.190
make very important
decisions but

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.860
the independent
businessperson is

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.610
responsible for his own
destiny or her destiny,

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.310
and one mistake can
destroy their family.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:50.140
They're not a cog in
a corporate wheel.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.070
So what I'm suggesting
to you is maybe

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.320
we can't be all
small farmers or we

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.540
can't be all middle class,
small business people,

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.870
but we need this
group to be present,

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.550
because without
this present, you

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.920
do not have these
independent voices

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.670
and we don't combine the
physical and the mental and

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:12.420
of people who take
responsibility for themselves.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.850
OK, so middle class
citizenship is

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:18.210
crucial in the history of
constitutional government.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.210
Unfortunately in our
generation, it's eroding,

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.610
and we can see it erode
in a variety of contexts.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.690
The first is for 10
years, average wages

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.520
of the middle
class did not rise.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.030
50% of the country dies
with less than $10,000

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:35.220
in aggregate wealth.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:39.030
Over half of Americans
die with credit card debt.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.640
Their buying
options are limited,

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.940
their choices on how
they live are limited,

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.570
their chances at home
ownership decline simply

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.160
because they owe a lot of debt.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.030
Nowhere is this more dramatic
than in student loans.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:57.060
When the student
graduates, the average loan

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:00.510
is somewhere between
$30,000 and $40,000.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:05.340
We have an entire generation of
students that are graduating--

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.620
often with therapeutic degrees--

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.280
and are not able to find
jobs that would allow them

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.040
to pay off this enormous debt.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.800
If we came from Mars and
we looked at the situation,

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.290
we would just simply say
you have tens of thousands

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:22.079
of serfs or indentured servants.

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:25.590
If they're not beholden
to their credit cards,

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.360
they're beholden to
the federal government

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.235
and the universities.

00:04:28.235 --> 00:04:31.250
[MUSIC PLAYING]

